From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:08:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/75] x86 DoZeroUpper32Opt: stop when an instruction writes
 the source or target register (#41813)

Fix proposed by the reporter in #41813: a partial write to the target
register ends the equality the scan relies on. Without it the #41813
program reports a clobber at -O3/-O4 on x86_64-linux and win64.
---
 compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas b/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
index e1147753..3e004cf9 100644
--- a/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
+++ b/compiler/x86/aoptx86.pas
@@ -16115,6 +16115,13 @@ unit aoptx86;
                     Result := True;
                     Exit;
                   end;
+
+                { If hp1 also writes to the target or source register (e.g. a
+                  partial write to a subregister), the registers no longer
+                  hold equal values, so stop searching (#41813) }
+                if RegModifiedByInstruction(FullTargetReg,hp1) or
+                  RegModifiedByInstruction(FullSourceReg,hp1) then
+                  Break;
               end
             else
               Break;
